WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.863 line:82%
Chapter 22. Speaking games. Eight activities that get every student talking.

00:00:07.292 --> 00:00:13.423 line:82%
Open "Activities and games", then the "Speaking" door. Here are all the speaking activities.

00:00:13.874 --> 00:00:22.003 line:82%
Taboo. Choose a lesson. The cards come ready from your book unit. You can see them, change the forbidden words, or add your own.

00:00:22.469 --> 00:00:29.343 line:82%
Teams are made by rows, so nobody moves. Open the waiting room. Students join on their phones.

00:00:44.832 --> 00:00:53.414 line:82%
Press Start. The app picks the describer fairly. Their phone shows the word and the forbidden words. The team guesses out loud.

00:00:53.868 --> 00:01:04.434 line:82%
Beginners get only two forbidden words, and some help to start. A student of the next team sees the same card, and taps Buzz if they hear a forbidden word.

00:01:04.899 --> 00:01:10.553 line:82%
Got it is one point, a buzz loses one. When the time ends, the next team plays.

00:01:11.008 --> 00:01:18.534 line:82%
Find someone who. Students stand up and walk around. Each phone shows six to eight lines from the lesson grammar.

00:01:40.147 --> 00:01:49.687 line:82%
A student asks: "Do you play football?" A yes? Tap the classmate's name, ask one more question, and write the answer. Each name only once!

00:01:50.152 --> 00:01:59.769 line:82%
The board shows everyone's card. Then press Stop: the class survey shows how many said yes, and Tell picks a student to report in a full sentence.

00:02:00.222 --> 00:02:06.950 line:82%
Opinion swap. A statement appears. Everyone votes: agree or disagree, with no middle.

00:02:22.754 --> 00:02:29.351 line:82%
Press Pair up. Each phone shows the nearest classmate who voted the other way. They talk for two minutes.

00:02:29.803 --> 00:02:39.569 line:82%
Then everyone votes again and writes their best reason. The board shows who changed their mind. When your partner changes their mind, you win a star.

00:02:42.477 --> 00:02:51.631 line:82%
Story chain. Groups of four or five neighbours build a story, one sentence each, from the same first line. Here, one group of four.

00:03:01.829 --> 00:03:09.308 line:82%
On your turn, your phone shows a word to use. Say your sentence to your group, then type it. The app checks the word.

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:18.848 line:82%
Then each group reads its story aloud from the board. The class votes for the best story, and all the stories are kept in the Record book.

00:03:19.310 --> 00:03:29.728 line:82%
There are four more: Info gap for pairs, Just a minute, Voice wall to record and listen at home, and Talk to Owl, a role-play with an AI on the board.

00:03:30.192 --> 00:03:38.548 line:82%
Every activity has help for each level, bonus points only when you press, and the results go to the Skill map, under Speaking.
